records.claim_root_cause_or_alert:
X0017_StrongEncryptionHeader.parseCentralDirectoryFormat() reads rcount (32-bit, ZipLong.getValue at data[offset+8]) and hashSize (16-bit, ZipShort.getValue at data[offset+14]) directly from the untrusted extra-field payload and uses them as the bounds of a nested loop whose body contains no work and no exit path:

    if (rcount > 0) {
        this.hashAlg = ...;
        this.hashSize = ...;
        for (long i = 0; i < this.rcount; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < this.hashSize; j++) {
                //  ZipUtil.signedByteToUnsignedInt(data[offset + 16 + (i * this.hashSize) + j]));
            }
        }
    }

The iteration count is not bounded by the actually available extra-field length (length/offset are passed in but never used to cap the loops), and the method performs no I/O, so the loop cannot terminate early on EOF and cannot be interrupted by stream closure; it is pure CPU consumption driven solely by archive bytes.

